ican. Hern, a Tulsa-area congressman, has raised nearly ten million dollars and draws about 2.4 million in outside support, while Democratic nominee N'Kiyla Jasmine Thomas has raised under sixty thousand dollars and reports only a few hundred dollars on hand. Every major rating service calls the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets price Republican chances near 98 percent.\n\nThomas, billed as Oklahoma's first democratic socialist Senate nominee, faces a steep ideological climb in one of the nation's most Republican states. A single August poll showed Hern leading 49 to 25, though it is now several weeks old. Republican infighting over the seat's transition has generated headlines but appears unlikely to change the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0081, "margin": -15.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0064, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0068, "margin": -19.0}]}